<title>MEXICO: INTERVIEW - Mexico sees grain imports waning in '97.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - Mexico sees grain imports waning in '97.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico expects grain imports to fall next year to 5 to 6 million tonnes, down from the 9.5 million tonnes that will be imported by the end of calendar 1996, Agriculture Minister Francisco Labastida Ochoa told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;Our imports of grains (in 1997) are going to go down to around 5 or 6 million tonnes,&quot; Labastida said, saying that the forecast was based on current expectations for an average Mexican grain harvest and normal rains.</p>
</text>
